iamf-adm-corpus
Copyright 2026 The iamf-adm-corpus authors

This product consists of original work. The ADM BWF corpus generator
authors its ADM/BWF structures (axml, chna, dbmd) as a clean-room
implementation written from ITU-R BS.2076-2, ITU-R BS.2094, and
EBU Tech 3285; the spherical-harmonic HOA encoding is computed from
the standard ACN/SN3D definitions. No EBU, AOM, or Dolby source code
is used or derived.

The measurement harness invokes third-party tools strictly as
subprocess oracles: the iamf-tools encoder and decoder, libiamf's
iamfdec, the EBU ADM Renderer (EAR), and FFmpeg. None of their code
is included in, linked into, or derived from this project.

The spectral-identity measurement convention (one unique identifier
sine per track) is original to this project's WP1 study.

"IAMF" and "ADM" are used descriptively as format names.

numpy and scipy (BSD licenses) are runtime dependencies of the
generator and measurement scripts.
